<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends flat in quiet market.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends flat in quiet market.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-10-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The taka closed unchanged at 42.5450/5495 to the dollar in interbank trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the taka remained stable throughout the session because of lack of demand for dollars due to weekend closure of most international markets.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates ended unchanged at 4.25 percent to 4.75 percent in a liquid market, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
